 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $5.4B in FY2025 [1].\nNet income was -$3.6B in FY2025 [2].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2025 was +8.4% [1] [3].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was +23.2% [2] [4].\nIn FY2025, net income growth of +23.2% [2] [4] was above revenue growth of +8.4% [1] [3].\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow growth of +54.6% [5] [6] was above net income growth of +23.2% [2] [4].\n\n## Margins\nGross margin was 2.7% in FY2025 [7].\nOperating margin was -66.5% in FY2025 [8].\nNet margin was -67.7% in FY2025 [9].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2025, free cash flow of -$2.5B [10] was above net income of -$3.6B [2].\nThe current ratio was 2.33\u00d7 in FY2025 [11], above 1.00\u00d7.\nCash & equivalents was $3.6B in FY2025 [12].\n\n## Red flags\nRevenue YoY growth decelerated across its three most recent measurable observations: +167.4% \u2192 +12.1% \u2192 +8.4%. Source operands: Revenue USD 4,434,000,000 in FY2023 [13]; Revenue USD 1,658,000,000 in FY2022 [14]; Revenue USD 4,970,000,000 in FY2024 [3]; Revenue USD 5,387,000,000 in FY2025 [1].\nLong-term debt grew +9346.8% from FY2020 to FY2025. Source operands: Long-term debt USD 47,000,000 in FY2020 [15]; Long-term debt USD 4,440,000,000 in FY2025 [16].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +8.4% in FY2025 [1] [3].\nWatch how net income in the next reporting update compares with -$3.6B in FY2025 [2].\nWatch how free cash flow in the next reporting update compares with -$2.5B in FY2025 [10].",
